I've written the plan for Day 261 (12:31): two task files and the issue responses. The commit step didn't take because session_plan/ is in .gitignore. The plan command allows for that (it ends in || true), so the files are on disk but not committed.

Done during planning, using gh only:
• Upstream ask filed as yologdev/yoagent#455. I read yoagent 0.27.9 anthropic.rs and confirmed the cause of #1206: the cache marker goes on the last block of an earlier message, and only empty text blocks are skipped. The bridge marker in bridge_breakpoint uses the same rule. So a refused turn that kept only its thinking gets the marker on a thinking block, and the API rejects the next request with a 400. The ask asks yoagent to skip thinking blocks when placing the marker, and gives the test to add.
• Posted a scope comment on #1206 linking #455 and saying what the yoyo side will do.

Tasks:
1. Part of #1206 (product): stop one refusal from killing the session (the 01:38 session lost its task this way).
   • Where: a new src/prompt/refusal_history.rs. When the last turn is a refusal, it strips the thinking blocks from that turn, or replaces the turn with a short text marker if nothing else is left. prompt.rs calls it after finish().
   • Tests: unit tests on the cases that must not change, plus a test with a request-recording stub that checks the second request carries no cache marker on a thinking block. Before trusting it, the test must fail once with the fix switched off.
   • Limits: the test uses only harmless commands and never contacts the real Anthropic API. The task stays "Part of" until #455 ships.
2. Fixes #1204 (product, the backlog-drain slot): make /config set temperature accept only 0.0–1.0, the range every run actually sends. A test ties that range to clamped_temperature so the two can't drift apart. Allowing values up to 2.0 for providers that accept it is a separate product question, so the task opens its own issue for it instead of leaving a note.

